IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ita-types`

-- Income Tax Act 1947 — ADMINISTRATION (Parts 2, 20A, 20B, 21 and the
-- administrative Schedules).
--
-- The few rules here that fix an answer: advance-ruling fees (s 108, Seventh
-- Schedule Part 2), who may consent to a prosecution (s 101), which court tries
-- offences (s 105). Everything else in these Parts confers a power or
-- describes a procedure, and is carried in NOTES.md's coverage table as inert.
--
-- Source: ../source/ITA1947.txt lines 843-1264, 32960-34112, 35119-35392.

§ `Administration`

§§ `Advance rulings (s 108; Seventh Schedule)`

-- Seventh Schedule Part 2 para 1(1): "(a) a non-refundable application fee of
-- $660 ...; (b) a further fee, calculated at $165 ... per hour (or part hour),
-- beyond the first 4 hours, spent in consideration of the application ...; (c)
-- an additional fee, of up to 2 times the aggregate fee under sub-paragraphs (a)
-- and (b), for the Comptroller to give priority to the application ...; and (d)
-- reimbursement fees".
DECLARE `Ruling fees` HAS
    `application fee`              IS A NUMBER
    `further fee`                  IS A NUMBER
    `most for priority`            IS A NUMBER
    `total before reimbursements`  IS A NUMBER

@ref s 108; Seventh Schedule Part 2 para 1(1)
GIVEN `hours spent`        IS A NUMBER
      `priority requested` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Ruling fees`
`the advance ruling fees for hours spent` `hours spent` `, priority:` `priority requested` MEANS
    `Ruling fees` WITH
        `application fee`             IS 660
        `further fee`                 IS `further`
        `most for priority`           IS `priority`
        `total before reimbursements` IS 660 PLUS `further` PLUS `priority`
    WHERE
        `beyond 4` MEANS IF `hours spent` GREATER THAN 4 THEN `hours spent` MINUS 4 ELSE 0
        `whole or part hours` MEANS IF FLOOR `beyond 4` EQUALS `beyond 4` THEN `beyond 4` ELSE FLOOR `beyond 4` PLUS 1
        `further` MEANS `whole or part hours` TIMES 165
        `priority` MEANS IF `priority requested` THEN 2 TIMES (660 PLUS `further`) ELSE 0

§§ `Prosecution (ss 101, 105)`

-- s 101: no prosecution under the listed sections "except at the instance or
-- with the consent of the Comptroller or the Public Prosecutor".
@ref s 101
GIVEN `consent of the Comptroller or Public Prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a prosecution under ss 37L, 37M, 37S, 45(5), 94-96A or 105M may proceed, consent:` `consent of the Comptroller or Public Prosecutor` IF
    `consent of the Comptroller or Public Prosecutor`

-- s 105: "A District Court or a Magistrate's Court has jurisdiction to try any
-- offence under this Act and has power to impose the full penalty".
@ref s 105
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the courts that may try an offence under the Act` MEANS
    LIST "a District Court", "a Magistrate's Court"
